{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01EAeusVq5zBCW9U71L9ipLR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a single-user personal productivity and R&D mission-control system. Grounded claims from the project docs:\n\n- **Purpose:** A personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty that lives entirely in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`) â€” no syncing, no siblings, no database. Markdown files are the source of truth (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files under `domains/`, daily `logs/`).\n\n- **What it ships (core app):** `anchor_gui.py`, a self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server that renders a browser dashboard on `http://localhost:8777` and writes directly to the markdown files. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) provides the same task operations and also generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Task management:** Full task lifecycle â€” active â†’ done/cancelled/saved-for-later/restored â€” across domains (academic, commercial, family, writing), with priority/energy/due/notes fields, quick-capture inbox, and per-domain views.\n\n- **Reliability:** A daily self-test (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) runs at 5 AM via Task Scheduler, parsing every file, exercising every endpoint on a throwaway port, and writing dated reports to `health_reports/`; failures surface as a red dashboard banner.\n\n- **The R&D control surface (its largest feature, built in four iterations v1â†’v4):** Turns each project into a \"Project Cockpit\" for trio-driven R&D work (the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill trio). It ships:\n  - **Real ConPTY terminals** per project lane (Research/Planning/Build), each isolated in its own git worktree, with a durable session registry surviving restarts.\n  - **Lane tiles with status lights** (green=working/amber=needs-you/red=crashed/grey=idle) that expand inline panels stacking a cached summary over a live, resizable xterm.js terminal.\n  - **Auto-generated, validated, cached summaries** (session + project level), an engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini), per-lane doc-role maps, cost/tokens/time rollups, a \"grass catchers\" idea board, and type-aware deliverable launching (skill/tool verify Â· service preview Â· program run Â· doc render).\n  - Ghost World Labs branding (\"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\").\n\n- **Dependency stance:** Python stdlib only, with exactly one declared exception â€” `pywinpty` for the optional ConPTY terminal subsystem (lazy import, degrades gracefully). `distro.py` enforces this by scanning for any other native/third-party imports.\n\n**Status:** v4 \"Project Cockpit\" was built by Foreman (9 waves GREEN, 637 tests passed) and merged to master on 2026-06-13, which also fixed a repeating-prompt terminal bug by unwiring the legacy v2 REPL from the cockpit."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"46e3dd73-d40d-47e3-bfa0-efc72a7a2f6b","uuid":"fa9c632b-f1d9-4884-88d0-d6939a8b1866","request_id":"req_011Cc1JA9QD9wbJnZhGArooi"}
